{"seq": 40, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current", "text": "Frozen v2 predictive result from #39: constrained decreasing centred leave-one-row-out RMSE is EXACTLY the series-mean baseline 0.788437 kcal/mol at all three triples. Every unconstrained fold slope is POSITIVE: ranges [0.306257,0.431777],[0.221156,0.272418],[0.358363,0.549539]. The unconstrained reversed-orientation fits improve RMSE to 0.694769,0.605271,0.724313. Thus this model has predictive score information in the opposite orientation; saying it contains no affinity information would be incorrect. Within-series Pearson r values (3/5) are +0.642/+0.498,+0.807/+0.595,+0.542/+0.499. Reference-respecting full slopes are also positive (+0.199478,+0.224388,+0.237360), with primary A/F predictions (-0.266722,+0.063075),(-0.401676,+0.187992),(-0.178970,+0.157868) kcal/mol: no pair matches both experimental negative central signs. Origin-fit fold RMSE is 2.103213,1.969900,2.144034; across the eight inherited v2 shared-source combinations it ranges [2.103213,2.103338],[1.969900,2.074832],[2.140176,2.144034], all worse than baseline. Centred fits are invariant under those B shifts. This completes the second declared-model test without combining v2 scores with polar-model calibration or treating scenarios as probabilities. No covariance-based rejection or independent model-selection validation follows."}
