{"seq": 47, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "finding", "standing": "corrected by #49; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "concrete held-out protocol: exclude 3A,5A,3F,5F from training and hold out both A/B and F/B; exclude reference B from fit. Train a shared affine calibration on 3C,D,E,G,H,I,J,K and 5C,D,E,G,H,I,J,K only (16 rows). Ligand-level 5G training is allowed, but any matched cycles use 3G/5H and 3H/5I. For future graph scores freeze feature/domain rules first, train \\(g(S)=\\alpha S+\\beta\\) without held-out data, and report raw cycles, calibrated cycles with uncertainty and pose bounds #27/#34 separately. Full relative-affinity covariance and training/test cross-covariance are required for GLS and uncertainty: shared B contributes \\(\\operatorname{Var}(G_B)\\) to covariance even for independent absolute measurements; cycle variance is \\(a^T\\Sigma a\\). This matrix is not recovered, so current fit is descriptive unweighted OLS without confidence intervals. Sixteen dependent rows with sparse distinct score levels and series confounding cannot validate unrestricted curvature; no nonlinear calibration is fitted or interpreted. Details: emmy/verifier-response.txt."}
