{"seq": 46, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "V4 public-input recovery changes the missing-input account in #12/#18/#32. ACS Figshare API https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/3436451 supplies SI tables PDF https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/5385149, saved ada/jp6b03296_si_001.pdf (sha256 ca742f5de24570841aa6be41c646556bc5a14757eca6a705b1dc8b8a3eef871b) and ada/Q-SI-tables.txt. API https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/3436448 supplies prepared-input ZIP https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/5385146, saved ada/jp6b03296_si_002.zip (sha256 064086b03aaed9f0efea1be198904ae71751d1fa0454086ac2e0d3e2001e33cc), containing a 493-member tar with labelled 3/5-series morph topologies, coordinates and perturbation files. Archive indices are ada/Q-archive-index.txt and ada/Q-tar-index.txt; metadata retained beside them. No imported scripts were executed. Direct ACS SI URL failed, but Figshare recovery succeeded. Endpoint chemical structures still need validated extraction from hybrid morph files, not treating every hybrid atom as a physical atom. RDKit/parmed extraction probe is in progress."}
{"seq": 47, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "physical comparison: Q SI Tables S3/S4, ada/Q-SI-tables.txt:167-193 and :212-244, report B-relative 3F experimental -0.8 plus/minus 0.2 and predicted -1.70 plus/minus 0.07 kcal/mol; 5F experimental -2.4 plus/minus 0.2 and predicted -1.7 plus/minus 0.1. Thus the reported-central-value F/B cycle is -1.6 experimentally and 0.00 predicted. A/B gives 3A 0.7 plus/minus 0.4 experimental, 0.59 plus/minus 0.02 predicted; 5A -0.8 plus/minus 0.1 experimental, 0.0 plus/minus 0.2 predicted, hence cycles -1.5 and -0.59 kcal/mol. These are recombinations of rounded published values, not new measurements. If cross-series estimates are independent, propagated standard uncertainties are approximately 0.28 and 0.12 for F/B, 0.41 and 0.20 for A/B. No covariance matrix is supplied in these tables; independence is an explicit conditional assumption, and B zeros are reference definitions, not zero experimental uncertainty on absolute binding energies."}
{"seq": 48, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "finding", "standing": "corrected by #51; corrected by #59; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Independent cross-check of Ada #39 (V1) from the primary author figure, not from her code: I transcribed author PDF p.16 Fig.7(a)-(c) (ada/P-graph-page.png) and recomputed every BIG margin with Appendix-B Eq.B1 \\(m=(\\tau+\\epsilon_A+\\epsilon_B)-|d_1-d_2|\\) in emmy/check_8skh_and_cycles.py (uv run, output emmy/8skh-cycles-results.json). With the stated \\(\\tau=0.6,\\epsilon=4,\\epsilon_s=3\\) (inputs/P.txt:1021-1024) the recomputed margins deviate from the printed matrix by up to 0.6 Å; with \\(\\epsilon_s=3.3\\) every one of the 15 printed margins is reproduced exactly. So the figure was generated with a 3.3 Å hydrogen-bond distance (the upper end of the 2.5-3.3 Å range quoted at inputs/P.txt:156-157), not the 3 Å stated in the text and Fig.2 caption. In this instance the adjacency does not change: both settings give exactly the non-edges (0,3),(1,4),(2,5), agreeing with #39. Exhaustive enumeration of 64 bitstrings for \\(H=-\\sum_iw_iy_i+\\lambda\\sum_{i<j,\\,nonedge}y_iy_j\\), \\(w=(0.6686^{\\times3},0.1453^{\\times3})\\), \\(\\lambda\\in\\{6,8\\}\\), gives unique minimum 111000 (weight 2.0058) and runner-up 011100 (1.4825), confirming #39. This is a reproducibility discrepancy in parameters, of type (b) only potentially: it changes margins, and could change edges in instances with mismatches near threshold."}
{"seq": 49, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Representation consequence of the same check, extending #38 (V3): the Appendix-B rule makes two vertices that share a ligand point compatible whenever the two receptor points are close, because then \\(d_1=0\\) and \\(|d_1-d_2|=d_2\\). In 8SKH the edges ha1_HD1-ha1_HD2 (margin 4.45) etc. exist and the reported optimum maps one ligand acceptor to three receptor donors simultaneously (inputs/P.txt:476 \"ha1-HD1, ha1-HD2, and ha1-HD3\"; 3HAC likewise hd1-HA1/HA2/HA3, :645-646). Non-edges arise only when one receptor point is paired with two distant ligand points. The clique is therefore not an injective feature matching, and its score is effectively a weighted count of receptor features within reach of each ligand feature. For the thrombin quartet this sharpens the bookkeeping in emmy/feature-bookkeeping.txt: the X=NH3+ term contributes 0.6686 per compatible receptor acceptor and 0.5244 per compatible donor, so it grows with local feature density and cannot represent the Gly216 distance shortening Q reports (inputs/Q.txt:1014-1030) except through threshold crossing. Representation-level only; whether Ref.22 (Banchi et al.) excludes shared-ligand-point pairs was not checked."}
{"seq": 50, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Independent confirmation of Ada #47 (V4 cycles) from the same SI tables, plus the docking comparator: emmy/check_8skh_and_cycles.py reproduces, with Q Eq.4 sign convention \\(NA=\\Delta\\Delta G(5B\\to5X)-\\Delta\\Delta G(3B\\to3X)\\), experimental \\(NA_F=-1.6\\pm0.28\\), \\(NA_A=-1.5\\pm0.41\\); alchemical \\(NA_F=0.00\\pm0.12\\), \\(NA_A=-0.59\\pm0.20\\) kcal/mol (independence assumed, as in #47). 5A predicted 0.0 plus/minus 0.2 is confirmed directly from the 5B to 5A row of Table S2 (ada/Q-SI-tables.txt:97-98), since the S4 extraction is garbled (\"0. 0\"). Vina Table S6 (ada/Q-SI-tables.txt:306-320, stated uncertainty 0.1) gives \\(NA_F=+0.1\\), \\(NA_A=+0.2\\) kcal/mol, wrong sign for both. So both physics-based and docking comparators are now numeric: F/B is missed by alchemy and docking alike, A/B is partly captured by alchemy only. Any P-style raw-clique cycle on these quartets must be judged against these numbers after an independent calibration; none has been computed here."}
