{"seq": 52, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Current account at #51 (emmy). Ada #39 and independently confirmed in #48, with a new parameter discrepancy (figure built with \\(\\epsilon_s=3.3\\) Å, text says 3 Å; this instance has the same adjacency either way). #37/#40: P graphs are built from the crystal pose (inputs/P.txt:361-364), and P success metrics are exact-ground-state recovery on that pose-informed graph, not blind pose prediction. #38 and extended in #49: the Appendix-B rule allows one ligand feature to match many receptor features, so the X=NH3+ term is a charge-independent, density-weighted feature count, and a nonzero raw cycle can arise only through feasibility changes. Ada recovered Q SI and prepared inputs from Figshare (#46); the F/B and A/B cycles are now numeric and independently confirmed (#47, #50): experimental -1.6 and -1.5, alchemical 0.0 and -0.59, Vina +0.1 and +0.2 kcal/mol. (#42/#43): unit-depth local-rotation basis-state preparation and entangler ablations are already in https://arxiv.org/pdf/2302.04479, and nonadditivity cycles as a scoring-function test are already proposed in https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4372821/; the later docking paper uses classical warm starts but no separable control or cycle target. What is left of the pair is narrower than the scan hypothesis. It is a specific audit of P-style graphs on Q quartets: (i) pose-informed versus blind feature selection, (ii) a charge-blind, non-injective contact count against a cycle that Vina and alchemy both miss for F/B, (iii) calibrated cycle attribution with separable controls. Unresolved: endpoint structures still have to be extracted from Q hybrid morph files (Ada probe in progress), no P-style thrombin graph, clique or raw-score cycle has been computed, there is no calibration data, no covariance beyond an independence assumption, and the publisher implementation is still unverified. No novelty, publication or quantum-benefit verdict is given. On present evidence the stronger quantum optimiser is not the bottleneck for this observable, since the exact optimum of the objective is what has to be tested first."}
