{"seq": 18, "actor": "ada", "kind": "idea", "standing": "corrected by #23; corrected by #34; corrected by #35; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Narrowed contribution: an exact attribution audit for substituent-cycle contact scores. Let \\(W_L\\) be BIG maximum, \\(V_L\\) maximum over BIG subsets with a jointly feasible pose, \\(T_L\\) returned valid clique score, \\(g_L=W_L-V_L\\geq0\\), \\(e_L=W_L-T_L\\geq0\\), and \\(D(a)=a_{5F}-a_{5B}-a_{3F}+a_{3B}\\). Then \\(D(T)=D(V)+D(g)-D(e)\\). Better optimisation cannot remove graph-relaxation bias; signed cycle errors can still cancel or worsen. #15 gives an executable finite positive g, not an observed thrombin g. This changes the scan question: establish joint realisability before calibrated thermodynamic comparison or quantum optimisation. A certified infeasible contact set C can be excluded by \\(\\sum_{i\\in C}x_i\\leq |C|-1\\); this is a higher-order constraint and changes resource accounting. A failed local pose fit is not an infeasibility certificate. Full working account and proposed F/B plus A/B test: ada/objective-audit.txt. Novelty, biological prevalence, quartet structures, final P implementation conventions, physical calibration and numerical uncertainty remain unresolved."}
{"seq": 19, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Independent cross-check of Emmy #8-10: inspected emmy/check_basis.py:1-54 and reran it into ada/emmy_basis_crosscheck.json. All 64, 256 and 4096 basis strings pass the stated independent-angle constructions; the literal negative-penalty Eq.(3) synthetic case selects illegal 11, positive penalty selects valid higher-weight 10. This confirms the algebraic checks under their explicit convention, not P implementation behaviour or optimiser performance. Established account: an executable BIG joint-feasibility counterexample (#15), constraint-induced coupling despite additive weights (#17), and signed attribution of relaxation versus optimisation gaps (#18). These support an objective-and-domain audit before spending on quantum optimisation. Unresolved: whether any such gap occurs in the actual thrombin quartets; final P code/signs and angle limits; structures and pharmacophore mappings; independent thermodynamic calibration and solvent/ensemble treatment; numerical experimental and alchemical NA with covariance; resource-matched classical comparisons; novelty against prior geometric docking work. No biological result, publication verdict or quantum advantage has been established. Working derivations and test proposal are in ada/objective-audit.txt; this is the best account attainable from the current material."}
{"seq": 22, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "superseded by #23; corrected by #23; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Practical refinement to #18: exact joint-pose optimisation is not required to bound a relaxation-cycle contribution. If a certified graph optimum W_L is known and a feasible pose supplies lower bound v_L^- while a global relaxation supplies upper bound v_L^+ on V_L, then g_L lies in [W_L-v_L^+, W_L-v_L^-], intersected with [0,infinity). For bounds g_L in [l_L,u_L], interval arithmetic gives D(g) in [l_5F-u_5B-u_3F+l_3B, u_5F-l_5B-l_3F+u_3B]. A nonzero lower bound on each ligand gap alone does not certify a nonzero cycle bias; exclusion of zero by this signed interval does. A failed local fit supplies neither a V upper bound nor an infeasibility certificate. This is a derived certification rule in native score units, not a computed thrombin interval. It permits an inexpensive first gate using feasible-pose witnesses and global geometric bounds while preserving #17 constraint-induced coupling as a viable alternative. It complements Emmy #21: even certified V and its cycle need not identify the ensemble free energy."}
{"seq": 23, "actor": "ada", "kind": "correction", "standing": "corrected by #34; corrected by #35; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Notation and domain clarification superseding #22: a feasible-pose witness must realise a valid BIG subset in exactly the domain defining \\(V_L\\) in #18. Given certified \\(W_L\\) and bounds \\(v_L^-\\leq V_L\\leq v_L^+\\), set \\(\\ell_L=\\max(0,W_L-v_L^+)\\), \\(u_L=W_L-v_L^-\\). Then \\(g_L\\in[\\ell_L,u_L]\\) and \\[D(g)\\in[\\ell_{5F}-u_{5B}-u_{3F}+\\ell_{3B},\\ u_{5F}-\\ell_{5B}-\\ell_{3F}+u_{3B}].\\] This conservative interval remains valid without independent ligand errors. Excluding zero certifies a nonzero graph-relaxation cycle contribution in native score units. Nonzero ligand gaps alone do not, and failed local pose searches yield neither upper bounds nor infeasibility certificates. These are algebraic bounds, not observed thrombin results; exact joint-pose optimisation is unnecessary if usable global bounds and feasible witnesses exist. Identifying free energy still requires ensemble information, as Emmy #21 is testing."}
{"seq": 24, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Closing account after reading through #23: reran ada/check_geometry.py into /private/tmp/q8p1-ada-geometry-recheck.json; all assertions passed and cmp matched the existing ada/check_geometry_results.json byte for byte. Established here are the synthetic pairwise-to-joint feasibility obstruction (#15; ada/objective-audit.txt:30-61), additive-score coupling through shared constraints (#17; note:63-73), exact relaxation-versus-optimiser cycle attribution (#18; note:75-89), and conservative cycle-gap certification from partial global bounds (#23). Source anchors remain P clique sufficiency claim inputs/P.txt:183-189, recovered author Appendix B ada/P-primary-rule.txt:39-54, Q ensemble definition inputs/Q.txt:399-428, F exception :903-913 and contrasting A case :1033-1045. This supports an objective-and-domain audit before optimiser transfer, with no biological or publication verdict. Unresolved: actual quartet structures/mappings and graph-to-pose gaps, implemented P sign/angle conventions and final publisher PDF, independent thermodynamic calibration including ensembles and solvent, numerical experimental covariance, matched classical and circuit resource comparisons, and prior-work novelty. Emmy #21 is a plausible complementary ensemble-identifiability test; no result from that test has arrived at this read. No additional molecular calculation or quantum optimiser was run."}
{"seq": 26, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "finding", "standing": "current; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "New finite-ensemble check: exact minima do not identify the binding cycle even after joint feasibility is repaired. With common reference measure and all microstate energies zero, changing only the 5F bound multiplicity from one to two gives \\(D(G_b)=-RT\\ln2=-0.4132275087\\) kcal/mol at 300 K; changing only its aqueous multiplicity gives the opposite sign, and changing both cancels. All four minimum energies and their cycle remain zero in every case. Executable emmy/check_ensemble.py and output emmy/check_ensemble_results.json:5-122 establish the synthetic calculation; derivation, partition-ratio formula and scope are emmy/ensemble-identifiability.txt:17-73. This is not a thrombin mechanism or a failure observed in P. If omitted microstates project to identical selected pharmacophores, an identical BIG optimum likewise cannot distinguish these cases, an explicit synthetic assumption. A universal scalar score-to-free-energy calibration is then impossible, but empirical calibration in a restricted chemical domain remains viable. Circuit Born probabilities and counts of cliques do not automatically provide molecular Boltzmann weights or state measures. Q motivates the distinction at inputs/Q.txt:399-428,1033-1047,1053-1063; the Q primary PDF was not recovered here. Script SHA256 ed30074c806c0b3364922f207a18b5d731f14696095c780a87ed1becc4080cc3; output SHA256 bd9cb4bc60770e61cef6fa1a07429a343dd825590745894ae82be47cd95aadbf. No novelty search was performed for this standard statistical-mechanical construction."}
{"seq": 27, "actor": "emmy", "kind": "finding", "standing": "corrected by #28; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Cross-check of Ada #15 and #22: emmy/check_ensemble.py independently constructs the zero-tau tetrahedron coordinates, verifies every pair separation is 5.1 Angstrom below 6 Angstrom, and obtains triple enclosing radius 2.944486373 and four-contact radius 3.123099422 Angstrom (emmy/check_ensemble_results.json:124-128). Combined with the centroid lower-bound identity in ada/objective-audit.txt:38-46, this verifies the stated geometric obstruction under the contact-radius interpretation. #22 signed interval is algebraically correct: minimum D(g) takes lower endpoints for positive signs and upper endpoints for negative signs, and maximum reverses them. It requires certified feasible-pose lower bounds and global upper bounds in a common domain; heuristic fit failure cannot produce the latter. No new biological pose, interval or prevalence result follows."}
