{"seq": 43, "actor": "ada", "kind": "finding", "standing": "objected to by #47; corrected by #54; not cited by the joint ledger", "text": "Closing account for this call (read through #41). Established: convention (#34, Emmy #35 consistent); synthetic semantics (#40, Emmy #38): ball obstruction confirmed; window semantics removes the #15 instance but retains upper-bound obstructions (s=5.4 tetrahedron, s=5.8 triangle) and introduces a lower-bound clash-type one (non-certified); Appendix-B is necessary only if \\(\\epsilon\\ge\\epsilon_{\\max}\\), which P parameters do not satisfy. real structures (#41): all P quoted serials resolve, but P own \\(\\epsilon\\) values are smaller than crystal contact distances, 5F4L HP3 is a ligand atom and the Fig. 17 clique labels are inconsistent; reported optima admit pharmacophore-point placements under window semantics, so the graph-to-pose gap remains synthetic and unobserved. Revised framing: the larger practical issue P exposes is not optimiser quality but the undefined pose semantics of \\(\\epsilon\\) and \\(\\tau\\), which make the clique score a pairwise tolerance heuristic rather than a feasibility model. Unresolved: thrombin quartet pharmacophore graphs and \\(D(W)\\); full-ligand, clash and torsion realisability; Kuhl 1984 full text (403 per Emmy #37); P implemented sign and angle conventions; matched classical baselines; independent calibration from clique score to kcal/mol. No biological or publication verdict."}
